restaurants that turn down all media?

08:04.140 --> 08:05.600
They all turned us down!

08:05.600 --> 08:06.420
You fool!

08:06.420 --> 08:10.000
Getting them to agree is your job!

08:10.000 --> 08:11.830
If you can't do that, then quit!

08:11.830 --> 08:15.470
It's guys like you 
who drag the rest of us down!

08:15.470 --> 08:16.950
Do you get that?!

08:15.470 --> 08:17.980
I'm sorry... I'm sorry!

08:18.310 --> 08:22.190
Oh, that'll be Director Urushibara 
from the production company.

08:22.560 --> 08:24.220
"Production company"?

08:24.220 --> 08:27.030
The station's creative teams 
can't do everything,

08:27.030 --> 08:31.330
so production staff from external 
companies often help out with shows.

08:32.100 --> 08:34.480
Urushibara's a director from one of those.

08:34.480 --> 08:36.160
Are directors important?

08:36.490 --> 08:39.290
You really don't know anything, huh?

08:40.540 --> 08:44.940
Variety talk shows like this usually 
divide the work among four teams or units.

08:47.130 --> 08:55.350
<b>Variety Show Staff Responsibilities

Writers
-> Pitch ideas, write scripts

Researchers
-> Do background research
\h\h\h\h(mostly interns)

Creative Director
-> Manages overall creative for the show

Producer
-> Person in charge / Manages budget
\h\h\h\h/ QCs final product

Assistant Producer
-> Handles casting and
\h\h\h\hprovides misc. support

Unit Directors
-> Produce and edit episodes
\h\h\h\hthey're in charge of

Chief Assistant Directors
-> Manage schedule

Assistant Directors
-> Errand boys</b>

08:47.520 --> 08:51.360
Several units work under 
the producer and creative director.

08:51.360 --> 08:55.350
A director leads his unit, 
and ADs help him out.

08:55.750 --> 08:59.810
Huh... I thought the same team 
made the show every time.

09:00.200 --> 09:03.780
Director Urushibara used to work 
for a flagship TV station,

09:04.190 --> 09:06.450
but he got himself in trouble 
and wound up fired.

09:06.450 --> 09:08.990
I hear he moved to his current 
production company after that.

09:08.990 --> 09:10.450
Ah.

09:11.020 --> 09:14.440
Even now, one of his ADs 
had to go on break,

09:14.440 --> 09:16.800
leaving just one to handle all the duties.

09:16.800 --> 09:17.900
I see.

09:19.480 --> 09:22.360
I'm surprised you're asking 
about the crew.

09:22.360 --> 09:24.130
What brought this on?

09:24.550 --> 09:27.710
I just thought I should be 
a good professional, is all.

09:28.480 --> 09:31.300
Shouldn't you be happy 
about that, Onii-chan?

09:32.070 --> 09:33.400
I guess you're right.

09:39.230 --> 09:41.590
<i>An AD's job is very simple.</i>

09:41.590 --> 09:44.060
<i>We do everything we're told to do.</i>

09:44.500 --> 09:48.030
<i>We go location scouting, 
research stories and topics,</i>

09:48.370 --> 09:50.240
<i>get onlookers to leave,</i>

09:50.560 --> 09:52.200
<i>pretend to be cameramen,</i>

09:52.200 --> 09:54.660
