13:41.340 --> 13:44.180
<i>And honestly, 
I don't really care that much.</i>

13:44.890 --> 13:49.790
<i>Because he's really good to me, 
and that's all that matters.</i>

13:50.720 --> 13:54.790
<i>He's always thinking of me, 
and he never leaves me on read.</i>

13:56.190 --> 14:00.500
<i>On rainy days, he comes to 
pick me up with an umbrella.</i>

14:01.650 --> 14:04.010
<i>He's being a great boyfriend.</i>

14:04.010 --> 14:08.360
<i>Personally, that's all I really need.</i>

14:08.360 --> 14:11.120
<i>Wishing for more would just be greedy.</i>

14:12.100 --> 14:16.380
<i>I hear he hasn't met Kana-chan in ages, 
and he's even gone no-contact with her.</i>

14:16.950 --> 14:22.840
<i>It's so overkill that it shows how much 
she's on his mind, which annoys me a bit.</i>

14:23.350 --> 14:30.060
<i>But I can see it as part of his process 
for sorting out his feelings.</i>

14:30.610 --> 14:35.550
<i>It tells me how genuine 
he's trying to be with me,</i>

14:35.550 --> 14:36.940
<i>so I can live with it.</i>

14:37.270 --> 14:39.520
<b>Kurokawa</b>

14:37.670 --> 14:39.520
What time do you start tomorrow?

14:39.520 --> 14:41.660
I have to be at the Fuchu studio at 9 AM.

14:41.660 --> 14:44.080
Oh, that's pretty early.

14:44.080 --> 14:46.460
Take a bath and go 
straight to bed tonight.

14:46.460 --> 14:49.200
I will. Thanks, Aqua-kun.

14:50.420 --> 14:51.220
Bye.

14:53.910 --> 14:57.110
<i>I was supposed to be a fake girlfriend 
from a reality show.</i>

14:57.630 --> 15:02.280
<i>But Aqua-kun the liar is doing 
his best not to lie to me now.</i>

15:02.860 --> 15:05.140
<i>That makes me happy.</i>

15:05.550 --> 15:10.920
<i>I don't hate the idea of gradually 
turning lies to truth.</i>

15:11.310 --> 15:12.180
<i>But...</i>

15:12.770 --> 15:14.730
<i>If he cheats on me with some other girl,</i>

15:14.730 --> 15:16.190
<i>he's a dead man.</i>

15:17.150 --> 15:20.690
<i>I know you're a chick magnet 
and you like it, okay?</i>

15:17.840 --> 15:22.650
Pout... pout...

15:20.690 --> 15:22.650
<i>I've got my eyes on you!</i>

15:28.070 --> 15:30.780
Me? Appear as a cosplayer?

15:31.310 --> 15:34.220
<i>Dig Deep</i>'s doing a story on cosplayers,

15:34.220 --> 15:37.560
but they're having a hard time 
getting people to appear.

15:37.560 --> 15:40.960
You said you were interested 
in the show, so I thought I'd ask.

15:40.960 --> 15:42.500
Listen 'ere...

15:42.800 --> 15:46.960
Sure, I do wear costumes 
for mag shoots at times,

15:46.960 --> 15:49.650
but I do it as a pin-up model.

15:49.650 --> 15:52.470
I've never worn costumes 
at events'n stuff.

15:52.780 --> 15:57.230
Profilin' me as a cosplayer 
feels like a lie, no?

15:58.080 --> 16:00.080
A lie, huh?

16:00.730 --> 16:02.280
I guess so.

16:03.630 --> 16:04.320
But hey.

16:04.670 --> 16:07.450
It's still a TV job, you know? 
Wouldn't turning it down be a waste?

16:08.500 --> 16:12.400
You've got an established character, 
and I think you'd shine onscreen!

16:12.400 --> 16:17.370
I hear <i>Dig Deep</i> has a great writing team 
and has lots of industry eyeballs on it!

16:17.740 --> 16:21.000
If this goes well, 
it might land you more gigs!

16:21.830 --> 16:24.840
Well, you've got a point there.

16:24.840 --> 16:27.200
Of course, it's only if you wanna do it.

16:27.200 --> 16:30.130
I'll be there as the cosplay reporter,

16:30.130 --> 16:33.240
and I just think it'd be cool 
to work with you.

16:37.040 --> 16:39.190
Lemme check with my manager.

16:39.550 --> 16:40.350
Sure!

16:42.280 --> 16:46.820
<i>I </i>have<i> been stuck doing pin-up shoots 
and not branchin' out much lately.</i>

16:46.820 --> 16:49.860
<i>So this is a good opportunity.</i>

16:50.420 --> 16:55.690
<i>But cosplay's a fragile world that depends
on rightsholders turnin' a blind eye.</i>

16:55.660 --> 16:58.870
<b>No Pairing Shots</b>

16:55.690 --> 16:58.220
<i>It's got a lot of community rules 
and etiquette to follow.</i>

16:55.910 --> 16:58.870
<b>No Low-Angle Shots</b>

16:56.160 --> 16:58.870
<b>No Street</b>

16:56.160 --> 16:58.870
<b>Photography</b>

16:56.410 --> 16:58.870
<b>Plug Gun Muzzles</b>

16:56.660 --> 16:58.870
<b>No Long Props</b>

16:56.910 --> 16:58.870
<b>Skin-Colored Tights</b>

16:56.910 --> 16:58.870
<b>Required</b>

16:57.160 --> 16:58.870
<b>No Unedited Photos</b>

16:57.410 --> 16:58.870
<b>No Uploading</b>

16:57.410 --> 16:58.870
<b>to Social Media</b>

16:58.870 --> 17:01.870
<i>This might get messy if I ain't careful.</i>

17:03.210 --> 17:08.170
<i>I always thought Ruby hated fake-y 
stuff like this more than anybody.</i>

17:09.880 --> 17:14.150
<i>I hope the dirty business world 
hasn't started to change her.</i>

17:15.350 --> 17:17.560
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

17:15.350 --> 17:17.560
<b>Today

Thank you so much for getting in touch!
However, I don't have a <i>Tokyo Blade</i>
costume ready for this year's Summer
Comiket, and I'm not especially keen
on appearing on TV right now, either.


I'm afraid I'll have to turn you down
this time. I'm very sorry!</b>

17:15.960 --> 17:17.560
Another rejection.

17:18.140 --> 17:20.210
There's gotta be someone good out there.

17:21.980 --> 17:25.860
Nii-chan, do you have a Type-C cable?

17:25.860 --> 17:28.580
Hopefully one that's 
Thunderbolt certified.

17:28.950 --> 17:29.780
Yeah.

17:29.780 --> 17:31.480
What's it for?

17:31.480 --> 17:35.240
I wanna see if I can make 
my 3D model move using VR.

17:38.940 --> 17:39.610
Huh?

17:40.180 --> 17:42.620
Mimi, I need your help.

17:42.620 --> 17:44.130
<b>Mimi's Room</b>

17:42.940 --> 17:44.130
What?!

17:44.130 --> 17:46.590
N-No way! I'm not going on TV!

17:46.590 --> 17:50.280
I-I only cosplay at home, 
and I edit my pics a lot!

17:50.280 --> 17:54.370
Please! Your cosplay account's 
got a bunch of followers!

17:54.370 --> 17:56.820
I think the director will be fine with it!

17:56.820 --> 17:58.060
Wha?!

17:58.770 --> 18:02.300
Besides, did you forget what I do?

18:02.300 --> 18:04.400
My voice would give me away!

18:04.400 --> 18:08.860
<i>Mimi Yoshizumi, my little sister, 
is a cosplayer and VTuber.</i>

18:09.390 --> 18:14.800
<i>VTubers are people who use 
3DCG or Live2D technology</i>

18:14.800 --> 18:17.620
<i>to sync their motion-tracked 
bodies to virtual avatars,</i>

18:17.620 --> 18:20.400
<i>which they then use to stream online.</i>

18:20.830 --> 18:25.000
<i>Major VTuber agencies have gone on 
to cross 200 billion in market cap.</i>

